    "id": "p13-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Determine how many positive integers can be formed with the sum of the digits equal to 12. Each integer may consist of any number of digits and may contain only digits 1 or 2.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "233.\n\nCount arrangements for each possible number of twos, from 0 to 6.",
      "worked": "Let $k$ be the number of twos. There are $12-2k$ ones and $12-k$ digits in total. For each $k$, the number of arrangements is $\\dfrac{(12-k)!}{k!(12-2k)!}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\sum_{k=0}^{6}\\frac{(12-k)!}{k!(12-2k)!}\\\\N&=1+11+45+84+70+21+1\\\\N&=233.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
